---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="Design Org AI Initiatives | Jeremy Hoover"
  description="Three AI efforts I started or led in my design org: a content-design agent, a shared knowledge base, and org-wide training. All three are now required."
>
  <article class="section case-study case-study--orange">
    <header class="case-hero">
      <div class="container case-hero__grid">
        <div class="case-hero__main">
        <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="back"><span class="back-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Back to selected projects</span></a>
        <h1>How I got my design org actually using AI</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I didn't wait for an AI strategy. Three times I spotted something missing, took it to leadership, drove it from proof of concept to required workflow, and trained the people using it. That's a content-design agent, a shared knowledge base, and training across the org.
        </p>

        <div class="outcomes-strip" aria-label="Project outcomes">
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Hundreds</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Designers using the content-design agent I helped build</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Three</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Efforts I took from idea to required workflow</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Owner</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Of the review process for the org's shared knowledge base</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="glance-card" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
          <h2 id="glance-title">At a glance</h2>
          <dl class="glance">
              <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Senior Content Designer. I led the efforts, own the KB review process, and train across the org.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>A design org with multiple teams in multiple countries</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Pattern</dt><dd>Spot the gap, get leadership on board, build a v-team, prove it, ship it, make it required</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>All three are active and required</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Collaboration</dt><dd>Senior org leaders, principal design managers, DesignOps, repository owners, reviewers, and subject-matter experts</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Internal adoption, VP-level recognition, and an internal showcase talk</dd></div>
            </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="case-body">
      <div class="container case-shell">
        <aside class="disclosure" aria-label="Project disclosure">
          <strong>About the evidence</strong>
          <p>This is internal Microsoft work. I redrew the diagrams with generic labels and left out anything that isn't public.</p>
        </aside>

        <nav class="case-toc" aria-label="Design org AI initiatives sections">
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#gap">The gap</a></li>
            <li><a href="#agent">Content-design agent</a></li>
            <li><a href="#kb">Knowledge base</a></li>
            <li><a href="#training">Training</a></li>
            <li><a href="#required">What required means</a></li>
            <li><a href="#reflection">What I learned</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>

        <section id="gap" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>The gap</h2>
          <p>Three problems, all at once. Designers had no shared AI tool they could trust and build on. The org's knowledge was scattered across files and wikis, and nobody was maintaining it. And there was no real way for people to learn how to use any of it.</p>
          <p>Fixing one would have helped. Fixing all three is what got people actually using AI in their day-to-day work.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="agent" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>Content-design agent</h2>
          <p>Everything content designers needed was spread across Figma files, wikis, and email threads. To get a decent answer from an AI assistant, you had to rebuild all that context every time.</p>
          <p>So I packaged it. I wrote the foundational files that gave the agent its structure: the content, how it's organized, and links between things that had never been connected. I was one of the first people in the org, and maybe the company, to set up content-design guidance this way.</p>
          <p>I presented it at an internal design showcase. Other people built on it and the agent grew. Hundreds of designers across the org use it now, and PMs use it for content design and accessibility too.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="agent-caption">
          <div class="before-after" role="img" aria-label="Before and after showing fragmented content sources replaced by structured agent capability">
            <section class="ba-panel ba-panel--before">
              <span class="ba-label">Before</span>
              <h3>Scattered content</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Figma files</li>
                <li>Wikis</li>
                <li>Email threads</li>
                <li>Rebuilt from scratch each time</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
            <div class="ba-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
            <section class="ba-panel ba-panel--after">
              <span class="ba-label">After</span>
              <h3>One structured agent</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Foundational files</li>
                <li>Connected content</li>
                <li>Reusable by hundreds</li>
                <li>Extended by the org</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
          </div>
          <figcaption id="agent-caption">
            <strong>From scattered to structured.</strong> A few foundational files pulled together content that had never been in one place, and gave the org something to build on.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="kb" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>Knowledge base</h2>
          <p>The knowledge base had stalled. Years of design knowledge sat in a system nobody was adding to or maintaining.</p>
          <p>I took the problem to a senior leader in the design org, who connected me with the design manager overseeing it. With that manager and a small v-team, I defined the approach, built the proof of concept, and pushed it up the org. VPs liked it, and it became a full initiative.</p>
          <p>Now the KB is required. Every designer in the org is expected to contribute. Once we got it to general availability, I took on the governance plan: how people submit, review, improve, merge, and close contributions and gap logs.</p>
          <p>I designed the whole process. That includes entry types and templates, a review rubric, workflows for contributors and reviewers, triage, who merges what, and how we bring in subject-matter experts when there's a gap nobody can fill. I also built skills and prompts in the repo that walk people through it while they're doing the work.</p>
          <p>I piloted it with a small group of reviewers, took their feedback, and fixed the process and the repo before rolling it out wider. I trained reviewers on the standard. I worked with principal design managers, DesignOps, and the owners of the broader design repo, where the KB is a core part of the org's AI strategy.</p>
          <p>I went from helping launch the KB to owning how contributions and quality work. I still run the process and keep adjusting it as new cases come up.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="kb-caption">
          <ol class="kb-stages kb-stages--governance">
            <li>
              <span class="stage-num">01</span>
              <strong>Submit</strong>
              <small>Use a defined entry type and template</small>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="stage-num">02</span>
              <strong>Triage</strong>
              <small>Route contributions and gap logs to reviewers</small>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="stage-num">03</span>
              <strong>Review</strong>
              <small>Apply the shared quality rubric</small>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="stage-num">04</span>
              <strong>Improve</strong>
              <small>Resolve feedback and partner with SMEs</small>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="stage-num">05</span>
              <strong>Merge or close</strong>
              <small>Publish trusted knowledge or resolve the log</small>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <figcaption id="kb-caption">
            <strong>How a contribution gets in.</strong> Templates, triage, a rubric, SMEs, and clear merge owners turn required contributions into knowledge people can trust.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="enablement-title">
          <h2 id="enablement-title">Put the help where the work happens</h2>
          <p>A process only works if people can follow it. We looked at office hours, regular support sessions, and a library of training videos. Those would help, but they all live somewhere other than where people are actually contributing or reviewing.</p>
          <p>I pushed for putting skills, workflows, and prompts right in the repo, backed up by the org channel we already had. People can ask questions where everyone already hangs out, or set up time for something specific. The repo gives the same guidance every time.</p>
          <p>That way it doesn't depend on a recurring meeting or on me repeating myself. And when the process changes, we update the guidance in one place.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="platform-title">
          <h2 id="platform-title">How this connects to my design repos</h2>
          <p>The agent and the KB are part of a bigger org-wide platform that lots of teams have added to. Together they give the org shared content guidance, organized knowledge, and context about the work we actually do.</p>
          <p>The <a href={`${base}/work/ai-design-repo`}>AI design repo</a> I built for my business group plugs into that platform. It uses the KB, the agent, and other org tools instead of rebuilding them. That's how org-level work ends up being useful to a single team.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="training" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>Training across the org</h2>
          <p>Building something and getting people to use it are two different jobs. I did both.</p>
          <p>I'm one of the main AI trainers in my design org. I cover content design, the knowledge base, accessibility, gathering context, and research, for design managers and ICs. I don't just walk through tools. I teach when and how to use AI responsibly in the work people already do.</p>
          <p>Some of that is formal sessions. Some is demos. When VPs came to see what the design team was doing with AI, I built those demos.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="required" class="content-section">
          <div class="reading-column">
            <h2>What required means</h2>
            <p>All three are now a required part of how the org works. That didn't happen because leadership mandated tools. It happened because the tools were useful, the KB was maintained, and people knew how to use both. I drove all three.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="conditions-grid" aria-label="Adoption conditions">
            <div>
              <strong>Content-design agent</strong>
              <span>What the org builds on</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>Knowledge base</strong>
              <span>Required contribution from every designer</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>Training</strong>
              <span>Responsible AI use for managers and ICs</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="reflection" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>What I learned</h2>
          <p>The agent, the KB, and the training are all useful. But what made them stick was doing the same thing each time: find the gap, get support, do the work, teach it.</p>
          <p>This kind of work doesn't show up in a job title. It shows up in how the org works.</p>
        </section>

        <aside class="pattern-cta" aria-labelledby="pattern-title">
          <div>
            <h2 id="pattern-title">Still running</h2>
            <p>All three are still active. The agent is part of the org platform, the KB is required, and the training keeps going as the tools change.</p>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <hr class="divider" />
        <nav class="case-pagination" aria-label="Case study navigation">
          <a href={`${base}/work/hackathon`} class="case-pagination__link">
            <span class="case-pagination__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Previous project</span><span class="case-pagination__title">Hackathon PM agent</span></span>
          </a>
          <a href={`${base}/work/fabric-cli`} class="case-pagination__link case-pagination__link--next">
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Next project</span><span class="case-pagination__title">Fabric CLI AI skills</span></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-study { padding-top: 0; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  h1 { margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  .lede { max-width: 58ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-12); font-size: var(--size-xl); line-height: 1.6; }
  .outcome { display: grid; grid-template-rows: 2.25rem auto; align-content: start; gap: var(--space-3); transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .case-study .outcome__num { align-self: start; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 11cqw, 1.875rem); line-height: 1.15; white-space: nowrap; }
  .case-study .outcome__label { max-width: 25ch; font-size: var(--size-sm); line-height: 1.55; color: var(--muted); }
  .case-shell { max-width: calc(var(--narrow) + 6rem); }
  .reading-column { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin-inline: auto; }
  .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 90px; }
  .content-section h2, .case-summary h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .content-section:not(:first-child) h2 { margin-top: var(--space-16); }
  .content-section p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .content-section ul { margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6) var(--space-6); }
  .content-section li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }

  .disclosure { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: 0 auto var(--space-12); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-blue-soft); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; }
  .disclosure strong { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: none; }
  .disclosure p { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }

  .case-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); }
  .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .case-meta dt { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .case-meta dd { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  .case-toc { max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-8) auto var(--space-16); padding-block: var(--space-6); border-block: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .case-toc__label { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; text-transform: none; }
  .case-toc ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 0; margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .case-toc li { --toc-divider: var(--border); display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .case-toc li + li { margin-left: var(--space-4); }
  .case-toc li + li::before { content: ''; width: 2px; height: 16px; margin-right: var(--space-4); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--toc-divider); }
  .case-toc li:nth-child(3n) { --toc-divider: var(--border); }
  .case-toc li:nth-child(3n + 1) { --toc-divider: var(--border); }
  .case-toc a { display: inline-flex; min-height: 32px; align-items: center; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.3; text-decoration: none; }
  .case-toc a:hover { color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 5px; }

  .evidence-figure { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-12) auto var(--space-16); }
  .evidence-figure figcaption { width: 100%; margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .evidence-figure figcaption strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); }

  .before-after { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) auto minmax(0,1fr); gap: var(--space-3); align-items: stretch; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: #fff; }
  .ba-panel { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .ba-panel--before { background: var(--surface-tint); }
  .ba-panel--after { background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); }
  .ba-label { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .ba-panel h3 { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); color: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .ba-panel ul { margin-left: var(--space-4); }
  .ba-panel li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .ba-arrow { display: grid; place-items: center; color: var(--portfolio-blue); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; }

  .kb-stages { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-2); margin: 0; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); list-style: none; }
  .kb-stages li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 185px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .kb-stages li::after { content: '→'; position: absolute; top: 50%; right: -0.8rem; z-index: 1; color: var(--portfolio-blue); font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; transform: translateY(-50%); }
  .kb-stages li:last-child::after { content: none; }
  .stage-num { display: grid; width: 1.75rem; height: 1.75rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .kb-stages strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .kb-stages small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.45; }

  .conditions-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); gap: var(--space-3); margin: var(--space-8) auto var(--space-4); }
  .conditions-grid div { display: flex; min-height: 140px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .conditions-grid strong { color: var(--portfolio-blue); line-height: 1.35; }
  .conditions-grid span { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); line-height: 1.5; }

  .pattern-cta { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-16) auto 0; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .pattern-cta .tag { color: var(--portfolio-yellow); }
  .pattern-cta h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: #fff; }
  .pattern-cta p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); }

  .divider { margin-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-8); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .case-toc ul { gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .case-toc li + li { margin-left: 0; }
    .case-toc li + li::before { content: none; }
    .kb-stages { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .kb-stages li { min-height: 150px; }
    .kb-stages li::after { content: none; }
    .conditions-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .conditions-grid div { min-height: 0; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 130px; }
    .disclosure { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-meta { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc { margin-top: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-12); padding-block: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-6); }
    .case-toc a { min-height: 44px; }
    .before-after { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .ba-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); }
    .kb-stages { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .kb-stages li { min-height: auto; }
    .pattern-cta { padding: var(--space-8); }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .outcome:hover, .case-meta div:hover, .ba-panel:hover,
    .kb-stages li:hover, .conditions-grid div:hover { transform: none; }
  }

  /* ---- Visual refresh ---- */
  /* before / after: two open cards with an arrow badge */
  .before-after { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 48px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); align-items: center; padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; }
  .ba-panel { height: 100%; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: #fff; box-shadow: none; }
  .ba-panel--after { border-color: rgba(17,85,204,0.35); background: #fff; box-shadow: var(--elev-2); }
  .ba-label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; height: 24px; padding: 0 0.6rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface-tint); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; }
  .ba-panel--after .ba-label { background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; }
  .ba-panel h3 { margin-block: 0.75rem; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .ba-panel ul, .ba-panel ol { margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .ba-panel li { position: relative; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; padding-left: 1.6rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .ba-panel li::before { position: absolute; top: 0.1em; left: 0; display: grid; width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; }
  .ba-panel--before li { color: var(--muted); }
  .ba-panel--before li::before { content: '–'; background: #eef0f4; color: var(--muted); }
  .ba-panel--after li::before { content: '✓'; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); color: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .ba-arrow { display: grid; width: 44px; height: 44px; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); box-shadow: var(--elev-2); color: #fff; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .before-after { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .ba-arrow { justify-self: center; transform: rotate(90deg); } }

  /* stepper: numbered nodes on one line */
  .kb-stages { --node: 36px; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; list-style: none; }
  .kb-stages li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 0; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: transparent; box-shadow: none; text-align: center; }
  .kb-stages li > span:first-child { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: grid; width: var(--node); height: var(--node); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; place-items: center; border: 3px solid #fff; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); box-shadow: var(--elev-1); color: #fff; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .kb-stages li::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: calc(var(--node) / 2); left: 50%; z-index: 0; width: calc(100% + 0.75rem); height: 2px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); transform: translateY(-50%); }
  .kb-stages li:last-child::after { content: none; }
  .kb-stages li::before { content: none; }
  .kb-stages strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.3; }
  .kb-stages li > small:last-child { max-width: 18ch; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .kb-stages { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; }
    .kb-stages li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--node) 1fr; column-gap: 1rem; align-items: start; text-align: left; }
